    "detailed_description": "<strong>NAHKA </strong>is a cry for help for those who can\u2019t speak for themselves. <strong>NAHKA </strong>is a Finnish word that stands for <i>leather</i>, <i>fur</i>, <i>hide</i>, <i>skin</i>, and <i><strong>pelt</strong></i>. <br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>is a game that stands for ecological values, animal rights, provoking story, engaging gameplay, and real-life horror.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.poster.avif?t=1671627701\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.webm?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.mp4?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br><br>This game shows the impact of fur farming from the perspective of animals. <br><br>Inspired by titles such as <i>Limbo</i>, <i>Inside </i>&amp; <i>Little Nightmares</i>, <strong>NAHKA </strong>is the ultimate feel-bad game about fur farming, an arcane, brutal, and unethical industry which should not exist today.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/8d6c22f9cbb97dcd25b3066fd05c476a.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>is a 2,5D puzzle platformer with heavy emphasis on atmosphere. The game explores the relationship between humans and animals by switching their roles. The protagonist of the game is a guard dog which is tasked to hunt down a white fox that has escaped from a fur farm. <br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.poster.avif?t=1671627701\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.webm?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.mp4?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br><br>During the game the dog is reintegrated to nature, and when he returns to the farm, he sees the world differently. The dog must rise against the masters.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/4066815a881a934e56d1a24397e62d26.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>takes place in the intersection between nature and agriculture. The game explores the differences and similarities of a dog and a fox. One is the man\u2019s best friend, other an animal bred for its fur. Horror elements are focused on fur farming and the effects man has on nature. <br><br>Although the game focuses on agriculture, NAHKA also explores other themes related to environmental abuse, such as deforestation, pollution, and extinction. Each of these themes are portrayed from a viewpoint of animals. <br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/c3872c76374b90259c2699b3019fef97.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br>The controls of <strong>NAHKA </strong>have been designed maximum accessibility in mind. The game introduces a very versatile control layout. The game can be played with one hand, either left or right. <br><br>The game has zero lines of text, as all the narrative is visual.",
    "about_the_game": "<strong>NAHKA </strong>is a cry for help for those who can\u2019t speak for themselves. <strong>NAHKA </strong>is a Finnish word that stands for <i>leather</i>, <i>fur</i>, <i>hide</i>, <i>skin</i>, and <i><strong>pelt</strong></i>. <br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>is a game that stands for ecological values, animal rights, provoking story, engaging gameplay, and real-life horror.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.poster.avif?t=1671627701\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.webm?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/0c0d041411e38f99fda31baffe230ffa.mp4?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br><br>This game shows the impact of fur farming from the perspective of animals. <br><br>Inspired by titles such as <i>Limbo</i>, <i>Inside </i>&amp; <i>Little Nightmares</i>, <strong>NAHKA </strong>is the ultimate feel-bad game about fur farming, an arcane, brutal, and unethical industry which should not exist today.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/8d6c22f9cbb97dcd25b3066fd05c476a.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>is a 2,5D puzzle platformer with heavy emphasis on atmosphere. The game explores the relationship between humans and animals by switching their roles. The protagonist of the game is a guard dog which is tasked to hunt down a white fox that has escaped from a fur farm. <br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.poster.avif?t=1671627701\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.webm?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/26ad8a4a0dcd4881fc75564d6818186d.mp4?t=1671627701\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><br><br>During the game the dog is reintegrated to nature, and when he returns to the farm, he sees the world differently. The dog must rise against the masters.<br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/4066815a881a934e56d1a24397e62d26.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br><strong>NAHKA </strong>takes place in the intersection between nature and agriculture. The game explores the differences and similarities of a dog and a fox. One is the man\u2019s best friend, other an animal bred for its fur. Horror elements are focused on fur farming and the effects man has on nature. <br><br>Although the game focuses on agriculture, NAHKA also explores other themes related to environmental abuse, such as deforestation, pollution, and extinction. Each of these themes are portrayed from a viewpoint of animals. <br><br><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1823810/extras/c3872c76374b90259c2699b3019fef97.avif?t=1671627701\" /></div><br><br><br>The controls of <strong>NAHKA </strong>have been designed maximum accessibility in mind. The game introduces a very versatile control layout. The game can be played with one hand, either left or right. <br><br>The game has zero lines of text, as all the narrative is visual.",
